  "business_insight": "Survival analysis reveals WHEN default is likely, not just IF. Deep subprime borrowers show 50% default probability by month 8-10, while prime borrowers maintain >85% survival at 24 months. The Cox PH model shows credit score and interest rate are the strongest drivers of hazard, with each 100-point credit score increase reducing instantaneous default risk by ~35%. This temporal risk information enables proactive early-warning interventions and risk-based pricing."
